cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its measurements, please cite the paper below."
title: "TACT: Trust-Anchored Confidence Tempering for Self-Consistency Voting in Large Language Models"
abstract: >-
  Confidence-weighted self-consistency beats majority voting only when a frozen
  model's confidence is calibrated in direction. TACT derives the vote exponent
  from the measured, signed, within-item discrimination of the confidence
  channel, and is bit-identical to plain self-consistency inside its shrinkage
  dead zone. The repository also carries the negative measurements: the stratum
  on which any label-free aggregation method can act is 2.5-7.5% of items
  across five substrates in two domains.
